WEBVTT

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.000
You can do it!

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.370
Heading into the world competition, someone 
will be chosen to add their strength to the team!

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:29.750
Who will it be?

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:36.760
Burning hotter and more 
blindingly than the sun...

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:40.770
Go and shine even brighter!

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:46.100
Great!

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.770
He's grabbed the slimmest of chances!

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:51.360
What concentration.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:54.900
Miyazaki's bucking bronco. 
Such magnificent dynamism!

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:58.630
The Wizard of the Waifu Board.

00:00:58.630 --> 00:01:02.800
A quick pan and he nails 
his Perforation Attack!

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:06.940
I don't understand the name 
he created for this move,

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:10.200
but it is truly excellent!

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:16.050
A freewheeling, science-type guy...

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:20.680
Is his riding based on 
instinct, or calculation?

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.650
Aloha oe!

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:26.950
He's been riding a board 
for as long as he can remember...

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:28.750
A born surfer!

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:32.700
With those discerning eyes, 
what does he see beyond the waves?

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:35.460
Justice!

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:40.480
His playboy era has ended.

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:43.130
In his new era, he's a man's man.

00:01:43.130 --> 00:01:45.890
Plunging straight forward 
with simple honesty...

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:49.030
His hot blood is burning.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:53.520
He said this...

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:56.630
"I'm not short on cash!"

00:01:56.630 --> 00:02:00.090
"But no matter how much money I save up, 
there are things I can't buy!"

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:03.490
"Waves and the feeling 
of being one with them!"

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:08.580
Right now, he is one with the waves!

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:14.530
<b>Masaki
Fight</b>

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:15.480
<b>Go for it!!
Japan</b>

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:15.500
You can do it, Big Brother!

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:17.490
You got this! Go!

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:19.490
<b>Go for it!!
Japan, Represent</b>

00:02:19.130 --> 00:02:21.300
Watch me, Sho!

00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:28.870
Take off!

00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:36.420
Amazing!

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:54.020
Let's Go Surfing!!

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:35.260
Isokichi! Morning!

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:40.320
It's a race to Sun Beach! 
Let's go, Isokichi!

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:54.420
You're too slow! Try to catch me!

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:00.630
Hup!

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:08.460
Huh? What's wrong?

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:19.830
<i>That day...</i>

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:23.850
<i>That morning... when I saw 
him flying across the sea,</i>

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:26.080
<i>that's when my fate was decided.</i>

00:05:26.730 --> 00:05:28.810
<i>The sight of him riding the waves,</i>

00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:32.040
<i>no matter how much time passed, 
it never faded from my heart.</i>

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:36.770
<i>It's like it would come in close, 
then retreat... just like the waves.</i>

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:45.570
You're really tanned.

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:46.670
It was Guam!

00:05:46.670 --> 00:05:49.560
You're lucky. I only went to Izu.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:53.580
Aw, man... Second term, huh?

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:55.800
Any chances for romantic 
adventures are over.

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:58.330
Studying for entrance exams 
is the main event now.

00:05:58.940 --> 00:06:00.580
It's so depressing...

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:02.680
Morning!

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:05.060
'Sup?

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:07.640
Good morning, Masaki.

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:10.090
Morning, Corgi.

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:14.730
Hey, Tanaka, there was a surfer 
I've never seen before at Sun Beach...

00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:18.250
Listen to me!

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:20.400
At Sun Beach, there was a—

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:26.240
For crying out loud. This bum.

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:29.080
Good morning, everyone!

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:31.140
Good morning!

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:34.130
Did you all have fun over summer break?

00:06:34.130 --> 00:06:37.960
Now, this is sudden, but I'm going to 
introduce a transfer student.

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:39.880
What? A transfer student?

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:40.630
What could this be?

00:06:40.630 --> 00:06:41.790
A transfer student?

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:43.330
At this point in the year?

00:06:43.330 --> 00:06:45.360
It's a surprise.

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:47.260
Akitsuki-kun! Come in.

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:48.380
Yes, sir.

00:07:02.140 --> 00:07:05.520
I'm Akitsuki Sho. Nice to meet you.

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:12.200
Now, for our second-years,

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:14.080
the way you spend your remaining time here

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:14.990
Surfer?

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:17.650
will be important as you look 
to moving up into high school.

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:17.350
I saw him at Sun Beach.

00:07:17.350 --> 00:07:19.230
He was super for real.

00:07:17.650 --> 00:07:22.230
Time flies like an arrow. The young soon 
grow old, but learning is difficult.

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:20.390
For real?

00:07:20.390 --> 00:07:24.320
I mean... He was seriously good.

00:07:22.230 --> 00:07:25.670
You never want to regret, wishing 
you'd done something differently.

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:25.670
Really...

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:28.670
"The show must go on."

00:07:29.070 --> 00:07:34.680
A literal translation of this would be, 
"the show cannot stop,"

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:38.680
but it is also used to mean, 
"we can't give up."

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:44.270
<i>We can't give up...</i>

00:07:46.990 --> 00:07:49.690
They say the Prince came here from Hayama!

00:07:49.690 --> 00:07:53.730
I wonder why he transferred in 
at this time of year.

00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:55.450
He's so mysterious!

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:59.280
Is Hayama in Tokyo?

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:00.950
Kanagawa, right?

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:04.960
Is Kanagawa... in Tokyo?

00:08:12.190 --> 00:08:13.720
Hey! Tanaka!

00:08:14.570 --> 00:08:18.740
Hey, Sho! Let's ride some waves!

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:23.220
The show must go on!

00:08:23.220 --> 00:08:24.730
Stop that!

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:31.810
"The show must go on" 
is a nice phrase, isn't it?

00:08:37.230 --> 00:08:38.900
We met at the beach, right?

00:08:38.900 --> 00:08:40.740
Y-Yeah...

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:44.650
I'm Masaki.

00:08:44.650 --> 00:08:46.420
Hinaoka Masaki.

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:50.000
I'm a second-year at the Oarai Minami 
Middle School, and I'm 14 years old.

00:08:50.480 --> 00:08:53.790
You don't have to say you're a second-year. 
We're all in the same class.

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:55.460
Oh, right.

00:08:55.460 --> 00:08:56.290
I'm—

00:08:56.290 --> 00:08:58.240
He's Tanaka Nalu!

00:08:58.240 --> 00:08:59.230
Nice to meet you.

00:08:59.230 --> 00:09:02.380
He's a surfer, too!

00:09:02.380 --> 00:09:03.950
Really?

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:07.720
I've only just moved here, 
so I don't know much yet.

00:09:07.720 --> 00:09:11.110
Will you show me 
the surf shops in this town?

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:12.260
That's an easy—

00:09:12.260 --> 00:09:14.030
That's an easy request!

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:16.640
We'll show you. This way!

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:20.030
Does he seem a little excited to you?

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:21.850
Hurry up!

00:09:21.850 --> 00:09:24.350
Let's go! To Fantasy Island!

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:39.770
<i>For some reason, it looked 
completely different</i>

00:09:39.770 --> 00:09:41.680
<i>from how it had looked until now.</i>

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:45.810
<i>For some reason, my heart trembled.</i>

00:09:46.300 --> 00:09:49.310
<i>For some reason, everything shone brightly.</i>

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:51.890
Welcome!

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:53.990
Oh, h-hello!

00:09:53.990 --> 00:09:59.570
Oh, Miss Shoko! You're the most 
beautiful woman I've ever met!

00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:03.580
Yes, yes. Your pronunciation 
has improved a little, hasn't it?

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:05.580
It's because I'm practicing.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:06.960
Very admirable.

00:10:07.380 --> 00:10:10.330
And this is rare. To think 
Masaki-kun would come here.

00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:13.090
What curious turn of events 
has blown you in here?

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:15.290
Is it because we've got a good wind today?

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:17.730
Huh? What's this?

00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:21.100
Nice to meet you. I'm Akitsuki Sho.

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:24.850
He's a transfer student! 
And an amazing surfer!

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:28.160
I'm Shoko! Nice to meet you!

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:31.250
Thank you. I've only just come to Oarai,

00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:34.080
so I hope you'll teach me 
about the waves and other things.

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:35.360
Leave it to me!

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:39.580
You introduced me to this place, 
but you don't come very often?

00:10:39.580 --> 00:10:42.530
It's because I don't surf.

00:10:43.900 --> 00:10:48.260
Masaki can't swim, that's why...

00:10:49.270 --> 00:10:56.710
He's never thought about taking up surfing.

00:10:57.260 --> 00:11:00.560
Masaki can only doggy paddle...

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:04.790
And from his doggy paddle 
came his nickname...

00:11:04.790 --> 00:11:08.000
That nickname is... Corgi!

00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:12.400
Really? I see.

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:16.050
Murphy! You bum!

00:11:16.050 --> 00:11:17.130
What's wrong with it?

00:11:17.130 --> 00:11:18.090
Huh?

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:22.330
Your nickname. It suits you. "Corgi."

00:11:22.330 --> 00:11:24.410
D-Does it?

00:11:24.940 --> 00:11:29.410
Well, I'm going to go home, 
then head out to Sun Beach.

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:31.420
I might do that, too.

00:11:31.780 --> 00:11:33.630
The waves are good today.

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:35.170
Sho-kun!

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:39.800
The shorebreak can be a little rough 
at Sun Beach, so be careful, okay?

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:42.120
I will. Thank you.

00:11:43.020 --> 00:11:45.390
Well, see you later, Sho.

00:11:45.390 --> 00:11:46.230
Me, too!

00:11:46.230 --> 00:11:47.060
What?

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:47.860
What?

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:51.940
I'll go, too!

00:11:56.690 --> 00:11:58.000
I'm home!

00:11:58.000 --> 00:11:59.540
Welcome back!

00:11:59.540 --> 00:12:01.190
Welcome back, Big Brother!

00:12:01.630 --> 00:12:03.370
Want some dried sweet potato?

00:12:08.220 --> 00:12:09.610
I'm off!

00:12:09.610 --> 00:12:11.120
Come back safe!

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:14.550
It's so hot, and he's still so energetic.

00:12:14.550 --> 00:12:17.210
He's such a child.

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:54.750
Sho's really amazing, right? 
He's the real thing.

00:12:56.880 --> 00:12:58.450
Say, Corgi...

00:12:58.450 --> 00:12:59.500
Huh?

00:12:59.950 --> 00:13:03.370
No matter how many times 
I've invited you, you never came.

00:13:03.370 --> 00:13:06.700
Why'd you decide to come today?

00:13:06.700 --> 00:13:10.020
Wh-Why does that matter?

00:13:10.020 --> 00:13:11.510
Huh...

00:13:11.910 --> 00:13:14.260
Masaki, you sure you just want to watch?

00:13:14.800 --> 00:13:16.020
You should come do it with us.

00:13:16.670 --> 00:13:19.200
Sho. I told you, didn't I?

00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:20.810
Corgi and surfing are—

00:13:20.810 --> 00:13:21.780
I'll do it!

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:22.760
Huh?

00:13:24.690 --> 00:13:26.530
Let's go surfing!

00:13:29.020 --> 00:13:32.790
<i>I didn't hesitate at all 
when I replied that I'd do it.</i>

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:35.450
<i>I wanted to ride the waves, too.</i>

00:13:36.430 --> 00:13:39.420
<i>I wanted to go beyond 
the waves and fly high...</i>

00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:41.040
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:13:41.450 --> 00:13:43.870
<i>I wanted to be like Sho.</i>

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:03.290
This thing's super tight!

00:14:03.290 --> 00:14:05.420
It might be a little hard to breathe!

00:14:06.140 --> 00:14:09.660
Couldn't you have borrowed 
one a size bigger?

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:13.600
But I liked this design, so...

00:14:14.730 --> 00:14:16.070
Done.

00:14:16.070 --> 00:14:18.420
Once you get used to it, 
it'll be easier to wear.

00:14:20.330 --> 00:14:21.420
Yeah!

00:14:22.680 --> 00:14:25.700
Then, let's start with paddling practice.

00:14:26.070 --> 00:14:26.920
Paddle?

00:14:26.920 --> 00:14:30.240
He's talking about paddling. It's—

00:14:30.240 --> 00:14:32.550
My big brother's going surfing...

00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:33.430
Huh?

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:35.230
Sakura?

00:14:35.230 --> 00:14:37.080
Hey there, Sakura-chan.

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:40.440
You've really grown up since I last saw you.

00:14:40.960 --> 00:14:44.940
Tanaka-kun, I just saw you last week.

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:48.320
Ladies grow lovelier by the day, you see.

00:14:49.090 --> 00:14:50.760
You know you can't swim.

00:14:50.760 --> 00:14:52.670
No one asked you!

00:14:52.670 --> 00:14:54.390
Are you Masaki's younger sister?

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:56.960
Y-Yes.

00:14:56.960 --> 00:15:00.080
I'm Akitsuki Sho. Nice to meet you.

00:15:05.260 --> 00:15:06.670
Sakura-chan?

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:10.470
Sakura? Hello?

00:15:15.220 --> 00:15:19.850
Akitsuki... Sho-sama...

00:15:22.950 --> 00:15:25.860
Okay. Let's do this paddling thing!

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:28.830
First, would you lie on your stomach 
on the board for me?

00:15:28.830 --> 00:15:29.860
Sure!

00:15:31.520 --> 00:15:36.140
Line up the center of the board 
with your own center line.

00:15:37.010 --> 00:15:37.870
Like this?

00:15:39.030 --> 00:15:43.380
If you line up your center of gravity like that, 
it's easier to keep your balance.

00:15:45.370 --> 00:15:46.160
Huh?

00:15:49.090 --> 00:15:50.700
Bring your chest up.

00:15:50.700 --> 00:15:52.770
Oh! And keep your legs together.

00:15:53.800 --> 00:15:56.670
And then, you stroke the water like this.

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:02.200
Don't tense up.

00:16:02.200 --> 00:16:04.740
You want to paddle in a relaxed state.

00:16:04.740 --> 00:16:05.900
Okay.

00:16:07.100 --> 00:16:08.470
Don't just use your arms.

00:16:08.470 --> 00:16:11.630
Imagine you're using 
your whole back to paddle.

00:16:13.650 --> 00:16:14.910
Like this?

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:17.910
Okay!

00:16:22.970 --> 00:16:25.230
Your wrists should be at around this angle.

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:27.980
Keep your chest high 
and look straight ahead.

00:16:28.580 --> 00:16:32.090
And then, on one, two, three...

00:16:32.090 --> 00:16:33.140
you stand!

00:16:34.710 --> 00:16:38.180
One, two, three!

00:16:40.150 --> 00:16:42.620
That's it! Looking good!

00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:46.190
Sho! You're really good at teaching!

00:16:48.010 --> 00:16:51.190
Then, let's go try it for real.

00:16:51.190 --> 00:16:52.380
Yeah.

00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:06.800
Like... Like this, maybe?

00:17:06.800 --> 00:17:08.040
Corgi.

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:10.860
Why have you suddenly 
decided to learn to surf?

00:17:10.860 --> 00:17:11.700
Huh?

00:17:12.580 --> 00:17:17.220
No matter how many times I invited you, 
you said you weren't interested.

00:17:17.220 --> 00:17:20.850
Well... There isn't really a reason...

00:17:20.850 --> 00:17:23.390
I mean, we learned it in class right?

00:17:23.390 --> 00:17:25.400
"A wise man changes his 
mind. A fool, never."

00:17:25.400 --> 00:17:27.260
This isn't what that means.

00:17:27.260 --> 00:17:29.230
Uh... Oh! Look!

00:17:42.890 --> 00:17:45.660
What do you think? Want to try going out?

00:17:45.990 --> 00:17:47.840
Of course!

00:17:47.840 --> 00:17:49.730
I'll try doing it like you do, Sho!

00:17:49.730 --> 00:17:50.760
Moron.

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:54.840
It's not something 
that can be done so easily.

00:17:55.380 --> 00:18:00.140
For a novice to stand 
on a board can take days.

00:18:00.550 --> 00:18:04.220
No, how many weeks? Months?

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:06.260
What? It takes that long?

00:18:06.260 --> 00:18:10.730
That's an exaggeration, 
but it is pretty tough.

00:18:11.320 --> 00:18:15.110
My older brother taught me. 
That's how I started surfing.

00:18:15.680 --> 00:18:18.320
I fell into the ocean over and over.

00:18:20.330 --> 00:18:23.510
But the first time I managed to stand,

00:18:23.510 --> 00:18:26.080
the amazing feeling of riding a wave...

00:18:26.890 --> 00:18:29.200
It was like flying up in the sky.

00:18:30.280 --> 00:18:33.590
I will never forget that feeling.

00:18:34.140 --> 00:18:35.600
That's true.

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:38.400
I see...

00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:40.620
It feels that amazing?

00:18:41.320 --> 00:18:42.600
Okay!

00:18:43.030 --> 00:18:46.350
The show must go on! Right?

00:19:11.370 --> 00:19:13.220
Hurry up and go!

00:19:17.160 --> 00:19:18.880
T-Tanaka!

00:19:19.850 --> 00:19:21.970
Tanaka and I are here.

00:19:21.970 --> 00:19:23.890
There's nothing for you to worry about.

00:19:25.550 --> 00:19:26.460
Right.

00:19:41.530 --> 00:19:44.910
Surfing... Let's do this!

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:01.880
He's got a good sense of balance.

00:20:01.880 --> 00:20:04.110
Must be from his dad.

00:20:04.110 --> 00:20:05.400
His father?

00:20:05.940 --> 00:20:07.280
He's a construction worker.

00:20:07.280 --> 00:20:09.330
Ever since Corgi was little,

00:20:09.330 --> 00:20:12.500
he's been playing in the scaffolding 
of houses going up.

00:20:12.500 --> 00:20:14.060
I see.

00:20:22.660 --> 00:20:23.820
Oh!

00:20:23.820 --> 00:20:25.320
A wave.

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:26.460
What?

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:29.790
Masaki! You're going!

00:20:30.850 --> 00:20:31.680
What?

00:20:31.680 --> 00:20:32.550
Paddle!

00:20:32.550 --> 00:20:33.830
Huh? Right!

00:20:37.180 --> 00:20:39.700
This wave is way too good!

00:20:40.200 --> 00:20:41.590
I wanna ride it!

00:20:42.290 --> 00:20:44.590
Look ahead! Go faster!

00:20:47.870 --> 00:20:49.600
The wave is huge!

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:51.900
If I fall, I'll drown!

00:20:55.270 --> 00:20:57.770
One, two, three!

00:21:12.070 --> 00:21:13.060
I...

00:21:14.590 --> 00:21:16.000
I'm flying!

00:21:24.190 --> 00:21:26.970
Sho! Tanaka!

00:21:29.920 --> 00:21:30.950
Corgi!

00:21:30.950 --> 00:21:32.040
Masaki!

00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:37.090
Masaki!

00:21:41.830 --> 00:21:43.140
You okay?

00:21:44.860 --> 00:21:45.890
It...

00:21:47.610 --> 00:21:48.890
It?

00:21:50.970 --> 00:21:55.540
It felt so amazing!

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:03.620
<i>What I felt in that moment... 
I don't think I'll ever forget it.</i>

00:22:04.730 --> 00:22:08.270
<i>The first time I rode a wave 
in the September dusk.</i>

00:22:09.160 --> 00:22:11.440
<i>For the first time in my life, 
I felt moved, passionate...</i>

00:22:11.440 --> 00:22:13.390
<i>and it made me tremble.</i>

00:22:15.020 --> 00:22:18.980
We can't give up.

00:23:48.990 --> 00:23:53.990
2nd Wave    The Ocean Will Teach You
